 {"sec": "ALL immunophenotypic classification · p215", "page": 215, "q": "Surface immunoglobulin positivity (S.Ig+) is a feature of ___ ALL.", "opts": ["Pre-B cell", "T cell", "Early pro-B cell", "Mature B cell"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Mature B cell subtype: CD19, CD20, CD21 with S.Ig+ (surface Ig positivity). (Book p215)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-027"},
 {"sec": "ALL immunophenotypic classification · p215", "page": 215, "q": "Which immunophenotype of ALL requires intensified treatment?", "opts": ["Mature B cell", "Pre-B cell", "T cell", "Common ALL with CD10"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Mature B cell ALL → intensified treatment required, in contrast to pre-B cell (good prognosis with treatment). (Book p215)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-028"},
 {"sec": "ALL immunophenotypic classification · p215", "page": 215, "q": "Mediastinal involvement with CNS manifestations is characteristic of the ___ immunophenotype of ALL.", "opts": ["Null cell", "T cell", "Pre-B cell", "Mature B cell"], "ans": 1, "exp": "T cell ALL: CD2, CD3, CD4, CD5, CD7, CD8 with mediastinal involvement and CNS manifestations. (Book p215)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-029"},
 {"sec": "ALL immunophenotypic classification · p215", "page": 215, "q": "Match the ALL immunophenotype with its CD marker profile:", "opts": ["A-4, B-2, C-3, D-1", "A-1, B-3, C-4, D-2", "A-4, B-3, C-1, D-2", "A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Correct pairs: Pre-B cell ALL→CD10, CD19, CD20, CD45; Mature B cell ALL→CD19, CD20, CD21 with S.Ig+; T cell ALL→CD2, CD3, CD4, CD5, CD7, CD8; Marker of good prognosis→CD10. (Book p215)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Pre-B cell ALL", "CD2, CD3, CD4, CD5, CD7, CD8"], ["Mature B cell ALL", "CD10"], ["T cell ALL", "CD19, CD20, CD21 with S.Ig+"], ["Marker of good prognosis", "CD10, CD19, CD20, CD45"]], "id": "PEDS-C47-030"},
 {"sec": "ALL immunophenotypic classification · p215", "page": 215, "q": "True or False — Pre-B cell ALL is annotated as constituting about 40% of cases.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — the classification table marks pre-B cell as m/c: 85%. (Book p215)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C47-031"},
 {"sec": "ALL immunophenotypic classification · p215", "page": 215, "q": "True or False — In the classification table, the mature B cell subtype is mentioned with the annotation \"and most common\".", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — the table records mature B cell \"(and most common)\" and pre-B cell \"(m/c: 85%)\", both as printed. (Book p215)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C47-032"},
 {"sec": "ALL immunophenotypic classification · p215", "page": 215, "q": "A 9-year-old boy with ALL has a large mediastinal mass on chest X-ray plus cranial nerve palsy.", "opts": ["Biphenotypic leukemia", "T cell ALL", "Pre-B cell ALL", "Mature B cell ALL"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Mediastinal involvement with CNS manifestations is the T cell immunophenotype of ALL. (Book p215)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 9-year-old boy with ALL has a large mediastinal mass on chest X-ray and a sixth cranial nerve palsy.", "id": "PEDS-C47-033"},
 {"sec": "ALL immunophenotypic classification · p215", "page": 215, "q": "True or False — The cytogenetic classification of ALL uses chromosome number only, without translocations.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — the cytogenetic classification is based on chromosome number AND translocation. (Book p215)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C47-034"},
 {"sec": "ALL immunophenotypic classification · p215", "page": 215, "q": "Odd one out (features belonging to the pre-B cell immunophenotype of ALL):", "opts": ["CD10 positivity", "CD19 positivity", "CD45 positivity", "Intensified therapy"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Intensified treatment is required for the mature B cell subtype; pre-B cell ALL has a good prognosis with treatment. (Book p215)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C47-035"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Bone marrow failure in ALL produces ___.", "opts": ["Pancytopenia", "Isolated thrombocytosis", "Polycythemia", "Eosinophilia"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Marrow failure → pancytopenia (anemia, thrombocytopenia, leukopenia). (Book p216)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-036"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Thrombocytopenia in ALL commonly presents as —", "opts": ["Lymphoedema", "Petechiae", "Jaundice", "Clubbing"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Thrombocytopenia (present as petechiae). (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-037"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "True or False — Leukocytes are always absent from the blood picture in ALL.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — exception: leukocytes may be seen in a few patients. (Book p216)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C47-038"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Night bone pains in ALL are due to —", "opts": ["Periosteal hemorrhage", "Vitamin D deficiency", "Muscle cramps", "Marrow infiltration"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Night bone pains occur due to infiltration. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-039"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Extramedullary involvement in ALL is seen in more than ___ of cases.", "opts": ["60%", "20%", "40%", "80%"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Extramedullary involvement: > 60% cases. (Book p216)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-040"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Infiltration of liver and spleen in ALL produces —", "opts": ["Portal hypertension", "Hepatosplenomegaly", "Isolated splenic abscess", "Hepatic fibrosis"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Infiltration of liver and spleen → hepatosplenomegaly (or splenomegaly). (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-041"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Superficial lymphadenopathy of ALL is best described as —", "opts": ["Painless with fluctuation", "Matting with sinus formation", "Non-tender, firm, fixed and confluent", "Tender, soft, mobile and discrete"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Nodes are non-tender, firm, fixed, confluent. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-042"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Unexplained cough or breathing difficulty in a child with ALL suggests mediastinal involvement causing ___.", "opts": ["Pleural effusion", "Diaphragmatic palsy", "Pulmonary embolism", "Tracheal compression"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Mediastinal involvement → tracheal compression → unexplained cough/breathing difficulty. (Book p216)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-043"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "SVC syndrome in ALL produces facial flushing/edema and —", "opts": ["Jugular vein distension", "Collateral veins on the legs", "Pedal edema alone", "Bounding carotid pulses"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Compression of the SVC → ↓ venous stasis → facial flushing/edema + jugular vein distension. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-044"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Match the site of extramedullary ALL with its clinical sign:", "opts": ["A-1, B-3, C-2, D-4", "A-4, B-3, C-1, D-2", "A-4, B-1, C-3, D-2", "A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Correct pairs: CNS leukemia→Cranial neuropathies; Testicular leukemia→Painless testicular swelling; Mediastinal involvement→Facial flushing with jugular vein distension; Liver and spleen infiltration→Hepatosplenomegaly. (Book p216)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["CNS leukemia", "Painless testicular swelling"], ["Testicular leukemia", "Hepatosplenomegaly"], ["Mediastinal involvement", "Cranial neuropathies"], ["Liver and spleen infiltration", "Facial flushing with jugular vein distension"]], "id": "PEDS-C47-045"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Clinical features of CNS leukemia include cranial neuropathies, seizures and ___.", "opts": ["Peripheral neuropathy", "Ataxia alone", "Raised intracranial tension", "Hemiparesis only"], "ans": 2, "exp": "CNS leukemia: cranial neuropathies, seizures, ↑ICT features. (Book p216)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-046"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Testicular leukemia classically presents as —", "opts": ["Painful scrotal ulceration", "Hydrocele with tenderness", "Testicular atrophy", "Painless testicular swelling"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Testicular leukemia: painless unilateral/bilateral testicular swelling. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-047"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "A 5-year-old with ALL develops a painless swelling of the right testis during maintenance therapy.", "opts": ["Testicular leukemia (extramedullary relapse site)", "Acute bacterial epididymo-orchitis", "Idiopathic hydrocele", "Testicular torsion"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Painless testicular swelling in ALL = testicular leukemia, a classic extramedullary site. (Book p216)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 5-year-old with ALL on maintenance therapy develops painless swelling of the right testis; the swelling is non-tender and transillumination is negative.", "id": "PEDS-C47-048"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "A 5-year-old with ALL has a hoarse voice and unexplained cough with dilated veins over the upper chest and facial puffiness.", "opts": ["Angioedema", "Superior vena cava syndrome", "Congestive cardiac failure", "Nephrotic syndrome"], "ans": 1, "exp": "SVC compression by mediastinal disease → venous stasis with facial flushing/edema and jugular distension. (Book p216)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 5-year-old with ALL develops an unexplained cough, facial puffiness and dilated jugular veins; chest X-ray shows a widened mediastinum.", "id": "PEDS-C47-049"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Odd one out (bone-marrow-failure manifestations of ALL):", "opts": ["Thrombocytopenia", "Leukopenia", "Thrombocytosis", "Anemia"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Marrow failure causes pancytopenia — falling counts; thrombocytosis is a rise in platelets. (Book p216)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C47-050"},
 {"sec": "ALL general features · p216", "page": 216, "q": "True or False — Hepatosplenomegaly in ALL is due to reactive splenic hyperplasia rather than leukemic infiltration.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — hepatosplenomegaly results from infiltration of liver and spleen. (Book p216)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C47-051"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "The definitive sample for diagnosing ALL is —", "opts": ["Bone marrow aspiration and biopsy", "Peripheral blood film alone", "Lymph node biopsy", "Bone scan"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Diagnosis is on bone marrow (aspiration & biopsy). (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-052"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "True or False — Bone marrow aspiration in ALL may be reported as normal.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — aspiration may be normal, hence biopsy is also taken. (Book p216)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C47-053"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "ALL is diagnosed when the bone marrow shows ≥ ___ lymphoblasts.", "opts": ["50%", "10%", "25%", "20%"], "ans": 2, "exp": "≥ 25% lymphoblasts = diagnosis of ALL. (Book p216)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-054"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "On the prognostic classification of ALL, the standard-risk age group is —", "opts": ["1–5 years", "5–15 years", "0–2 years", "2–10 years"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Standard risk: age 2–10 years; high risk: ≤ 1 yr and > 10 yrs. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-055"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Which initial WBC count places a child with ALL in the high-risk group?", "opts": ["> 50,000/mm³", "< 50,000/mm³", "> 10,000/mm³", "< 5,000/mm³"], "ans": 0, "exp": "High risk: initial WBC > 50,000/mm³ (standard risk < 50,000/mm³). (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-056"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Regarding gender and ALL prognosis —", "opts": ["Only males develop ALL", "Females have standard risk and males high risk", "Males have standard risk and females high risk", "Gender does not influence prognosis"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Standard risk/good prognosis: female; high risk/poor prognosis: males. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-057"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "CNS involvement at diagnosis puts a child with ALL in the ___ group.", "opts": ["Intermediate risk", "No-risk category", "High risk/poor prognosis", "Standard risk/good prognosis"], "ans": 2, "exp": "CNS involvement absent = standard risk; present = high risk. (Book p216)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-058"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Which ALL subtype belongs to the good-prognosis group?", "opts": ["B cell", "T cell", "T cell with CNS disease", "Pre-B cell"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Subtypes: pre-B cell = standard risk; B cell and T cell = high risk. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-059"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Hyperdiploidy in ALL is defined as the presence of —", "opts": ["> 50 chromosomes", "< 44 chromosomes", "45 chromosomes", "55 chromosomes with t(9;22)"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Cytogenetics: hyperdiploidy (> 50 chromosomes) and trisomy 4, 10 are standard-risk findings. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-060"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Trisomy of chromosomes ___ in ALL carries a good prognosis.", "opts": ["9 and 22", "4 and 10", "5 and 7", "8 and 21"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Trisomy 4, 10 = standard risk/good prognosis; monosomy 5/7 belongs to AML risk stratification. (Book p216)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-061"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Hypodiploidy in ALL refers to —", "opts": ["< 50 chromosomes", "44–46 chromosomes", "< 44 chromosomes", "< 46 chromosomes"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Hypodiploidy (< 44 chromosome) is a high-risk cytogenetic feature. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-062"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "The Philadelphia chromosome in ALL is formed by translocation ___.", "opts": ["t(4;11)", "t(8;21)", "t(15;17)", "t(9;22)"], "ans": 3, "exp": "t(9;22) → Philadelphia chromosome = high risk. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-063"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Infantile leukemia with t(4;11) occurs in children —", "opts": ["< 1 year old", "> 10 years old", "2–10 years old", "5–15 years old"], "ans": 0, "exp": "t(4;11) = infantile leukemia (< 1 yr old), a high-risk translocation. (Book p216)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-064"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Match the ALL prognostic factor with its standard-risk value:", "opts": ["A-3, B-2, C-1, D-4", "A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1", "A-4, B-1, C-3, D-2", "A-4, B-1, C-2, D-3"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Correct pairs: Age→2–10 years; Gender→Female; Initial WBC count→< 50,000/mm³; Cytogenetics→Hyperdiploidy (> 50 chromosomes). (Book p216)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Age", "Hyperdiploidy (> 50 chromosomes)"], ["Gender", "2–10 years"], ["Initial WBC count", "Female"], ["Cytogenetics", "< 50,000/mm³"]], "id": "PEDS-C47-065"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Match the ALL prognostic factor with the value that marks high risk:", "opts": ["A-2, B-4, C-3, D-1", "A-1, B-3, C-4, D-2", "A-4, B-2, C-1, D-3", "A-2, B-1, C-4, D-3"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Correct pairs: Age→≤ 1 yr and > 10 yrs; CNS involvement→Present; Subtypes→B cell and T cell; Translocation→t(9. (Book p216)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Age", "Present"], ["CNS involvement", "≤ 1 yr and > 10 yrs"], ["Subtypes", "t(9"], ["Translocation", "B cell and T cell"]], "id": "PEDS-C47-066"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "A 3-year-old girl with ALL has a WBC count of 12,000/mm³, pre-B immunophenotype, no CNS disease and marrow hyperdiploidy.", "opts": ["High risk/poor prognosis", "Intermediate risk", "Cannot be classified", "Standard risk/good prognosis"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Female, age 2–10 y, WBC < 50,000, pre-B cell and hyperdiploidy all fall in the standard-risk column. (Book p216)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 3-year-old girl with ALL has WBC 12,000/mm³, pre-B cell immunophenotype, no CNS involvement and marrow showing hyperdiploidy (> 50 chromosomes).", "id": "PEDS-C47-067"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "An 11-month-old boy with ALL has WBC 180,000/mm³ and marrow showing t(4;11).", "opts": ["High risk/poor prognosis", "Standard risk/good prognosis", "Intermediate risk", "Good prognosis with chemotherapy alone"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Age ≤ 1 yr, WBC > 50,000/mm³ and t(4;11) infantile leukemia all place him in the high-risk group. (Book p216)", "type": "case", "stem": "An 11-month-old boy with ALL has a WBC count of 180,000/mm³ and marrow cytogenetics showing t(4;11).", "id": "PEDS-C47-068"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "True or False — CD10 positivity in pre-B cell ALL is a marker of poor prognosis.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — CD10 is the marker of good prognosis in pre-B cell ALL. (Book p215–216)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C47-069"},
 {"sec": "ALL diagnosis and prognosis · p216", "page": 216, "q": "Odd one out (high-risk prognostic features in ALL):", "opts": ["CNS involvement at diagnosis", "Hypodiploidy (< 44 chromosomes)", "Initial WBC count < 50,000/mm³", "Age ≤ 1 year"], "ans": 2, "exp": "A WBC count below 50,000/mm³ is a standard-risk feature; the rest mark high risk. (Book p216)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C47-070"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "The four phases of ALL treatment in order are —", "opts": ["Induction → consolidation → maintenance → prophylactic CNS therapy", "Consolidation → induction → maintenance → prophylactic CNS therapy", "Maintenance → induction → consolidation → prophylactic CNS therapy", "Induction → prophylactic CNS therapy → consolidation → maintenance"], "ans": 3, "exp": "The treatment table runs Phase I induction, II prophylactic CNS therapy, III consolidation (intensification), IV maintenance. (Book p217)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-071"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "The goal of the induction phase in ALL is —", "opts": ["To induce remission", "To prevent relapse", "To treat subclinical CNS involvement", "To sustain an existing remission"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Phase I induction: goal is to induce remission and look for response. (Book p217)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-072"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "The four drugs of induction phase in ALL are prednisolone, L-asparaginase, vincristine and ___.", "opts": ["Etoposide", "Anthracycline", "Cyclophosphamide", "6-mercaptopurine"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Induction medications: prednisolone, L-asparaginase, anthracycline, vincristine. (Book p217)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-073"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "A \"good response\" at the end of ALL induction is indicated by a fall in WBC count with —", "opts": ["Reduced blast count in blood alone", "Normalisation of the platelet count only", "No blast cells in bone marrow and circulation", "Persisting blasts only in the marrow"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Good response = ↓ WBC count with no blast cells in bone marrow and circulation → good prognosis. (Book p217)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-074"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "True or False — A good response to induction therapy in ALL predicts a good prognosis.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — good response → good prognosis; the response is assessed as part of the induction phase. (Book p217)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C47-075"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "Minimal residual disease (MRD) in ALL cannot be detected by ___.", "opts": ["Conventional methods", "Flow cytometry", "PCR", "Bone marrow biopsy"], "ans": 0, "exp": "MRD cannot be detected by conventional methods; it is tested by flow cytometry/PCR. (Book p217)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-076"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "Which investigations are used to test for minimal residual disease in ALL?", "opts": ["Lumbar puncture cytology alone", "Flow cytometry and PCR", "Peripheral smear and ESR", "Bone scan and MRI"], "ans": 1, "exp": "MRD test: flow cytometry/PCR. (Book p217)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-077"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "True or False — Presence of minimal residual disease after therapy indicates a good prognosis.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — NO minimal residual disease indicates good prognosis; MRD positivity is adverse. (Book p217)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C47-078"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "Phase II of ALL treatment is prophylactic CNS therapy with the goal of —", "opts": ["Preventing marrow relapse only", "Reducing tumour bulk before induction", "Differentiating malignant cells", "Treating subclinical CNS involvement"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Phase II: to treat subclinical CNS involvement. (Book p217)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-079"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "Prophylactic CNS therapy in ALL is given as ___.", "opts": ["Intrathecal methotrexate", "Intravenous vincristine", "Oral 6-mercaptopurine", "Intrathecal cytosine-arabinoside"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Prophylactic CNS therapy = intrathecal methotrexate. (Book p217)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-080"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "Phase III of ALL treatment is called the ___ phase.", "opts": ["Prophylactic CNS", "Consolidation", "Induction", "Maintenance"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Phase III = consolidation (intensification) phase. (Book p217)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-081"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "The twin goals of the consolidation phase in ALL are to tackle drug resistance and to ___.", "opts": ["Differentiate blasts", "Prevent marrow aplasia", "Sustain remission", "Reduce CNS deposits"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Consolidation: tackle drug resistance & sustain remission. (Book p217)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-082"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "Which drug is used in the consolidation phase but NOT in the induction phase of ALL?", "opts": ["Vincristine", "Prednisolone", "L-asparaginase", "Cyclophosphamide"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Consolidation drugs: methotrexate, epipodophyllotoxin, cyclophosphamide, cytosine-arabinoside; vincristine/prednisolone/L-asparaginase belong to induction. (Book p217)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-083"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "Epipodophyllotoxin is used in which phase of ALL therapy?", "opts": ["Consolidation (intensification)", "Induction", "Prophylactic CNS therapy", "Maintenance"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Epipodophyllotoxin is listed among consolidation-phase medications. (Book p217)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-084"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "In the maintenance phase of ALL, chemotherapy is given once a week for ___.", "opts": ["3 years", "A year", "6 months", "2 years"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Maintenance phase: once a week for a yr. (Book p217)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-085"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "The goal of the maintenance phase in ALL is —", "opts": ["To treat subclinical CNS disease", "To intensify therapy", "To prevent relapse", "To induce remission"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Phase IV maintenance: to prevent relapse. (Book p217)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-086"},
 {"sec": "ALL treatment phases · p217", "page": 217, "q": "Which pair of drugs constitutes maintenance therapy in ALL?", "opts": ["Cyclophosphamide and etoposide", "Daunorubicin and cytosine arabinoside", "ATRA and tretinoin", "6-mercaptopurine and methotrexate"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Maintenance medications: 6-mercaptopurine, methotrexate. (Book p217)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-087"},
