 {"sec": "LCH features and spectrum · p220–221", "page": 220, "q": "A skin lesion of LCH that mimics seborrheic dermatitis but does not respond to its treatment is called ___.", "opts": ["Nappy rash", "Erythema multiforme", "Seborrheic keratosis", "Cradle cap"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Skin lesions show scales with discharge, mimic seborrheic dermatitis and do not respond to its treatment (cradle cap). (Book p220)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-211"},
 {"sec": "LCH features and spectrum · p220–221", "page": 220, "q": "In LCH, pituitary infiltration destroys the stalk and blocks release of vasopressin/ADH from ___ granules, causing diabetes insipidus.", "opts": ["Posterior pituitary", "Anterior pituitary", "Hypothalamic", "Pineal"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Stalk destruction blocks vasopressin/ADH release from posterior pituitary granules → diabetes insipidus. (Book p220)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C47-212"},
 {"sec": "LCH features and spectrum · p220–221", "page": 220, "q": "The MRI finding described in LCH with pituitary involvement is —", "opts": ["Thickened infundibulum with a bright spot", "Loss of the bright spot in the posterior pituitary", "Empty sella with a normal posterior bright spot", "Pituitary macroadenoma"], "ans": 1, "exp": "MRI: loss of the bright spot in the posterior pituitary. (Book p220)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-213"},
 {"sec": "LCH features and spectrum · p220–221", "page": 220, "q": "Apart from bone, skin and pituitary, LCH may involve the —", "opts": ["Adrenal glands and gonads", "Peripheral nerves and muscles", "Lymph nodes and hepatosplenic system", "Retina and cornea only"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Sites 4 and 5: lymphadenopathy and hepatosplenomegaly. (Book p220)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C47-214"},
