 {"sec": "LCH features and spectrum · p220–221", "page": 221, "q": "A 4-year-old presents with a punched-out skull defect, polyuria with dilute urine and unilateral proptosis.", "opts": ["Eosinophilic granuloma", "Letterer-Siwe disease", "Nephrogenic diabetes insipidus", "Hand-Schüller-Christian disease"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Skull defect + diabetes insipidus + exophthalmos = the Hand-Schüller-Christian triad (2–6 years). (Book p221)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 4-year-old presents with a punched-out lytic skull defect, polyuria with dilute urine and unilateral proptosis; biopsy of the skull lesion shows Langerhans-like cells.", "id": "PEDS-C47-223"},
